# web

## public feed
- label: the public v1 usage feed serves the same published snapshot as the dashboard
  command: bun test packages/web/test/public-usage-api.test.ts
  tags: [implemented]

## providers
- label: NanoClaw session usage is collected as a separate turquoise provider
  command: grep -Fq '"nanoclaw"' packages/cli/src/lib/interfaces.ts && grep -Fq 'loadNanoClawRows' packages/cli/src/providers.ts && grep -Fq 'NanoClaw' packages/web/lib/analytics.ts && grep -Fq '"nanoclaw",' packages/web/scripts/publish-usage.ts && grep -Fq 'accent: "#22d3ee"' packages/web/lib/analytics.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the CLI counts Codex sessions stored as zstd-compressed rollout-*.jsonl.zst files once, with a plain .jsonl hiding its compressed sibling
  command: (bun run --cwd packages/cli build >/dev/null 2>&1; true) && bunx tsx --test --test-name-pattern 'Codex reads .jsonl.zst|mix plain and compressed' packages/cli/test/cli.test.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: no CLI provider emits zero-total daily rows, so activity-only Claude days left by pruned transcripts cannot overwrite published token history
  command: (bun run --cwd packages/cli build >/dev/null 2>&1; true) && bunx tsx --test --test-name-pattern 'never activity-only zero rows' packages/cli/test/cli.test.ts && grep -Fq 'filter(([, entry]) => entry.tokens.total > 0)' packages/cli/src/lib/utils.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the web token report recognizes Antigravity CLI as the agy provider when agy usage is present
  command: grep -q '"agy"' packages/web/lib/types.ts && grep -q 'Antigravity CLI' packages/web/lib/analytics.ts && grep -q '"agy"' packages/web/scripts/publish-usage.ts && grep -q 'agy:' packages/cli/src/graph.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the web token report presents Gemini CLI history as part of the Antigravity CLI provider row
  command: grep -Fq 'agy: "Antigravity CLI"' packages/web/lib/analytics.ts && ! grep -R 'Gemini CLI successor' packages/cli/src packages/web/app packages/web/lib packages/web/scripts packages/web/test packages/cli/test
  tags: [implemented]
- the CLI reads Antigravity CLI generation metadata from ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/conversations and publishes agy token totals when usage blobs are present @implemented
- the web report only shows the Antigravity CLI no-data state when neither legacy Gemini CLI nor current agy rows are published @implemented
- label: the published web report folds legacy Gemini CLI and current agy usage into one Antigravity CLI provider row instead of describing agy as a Gemini CLI successor
  command: bunx tsx --test --test-name-pattern 'folds Gemini CLI history' packages/web/test/publish-usage.test.ts && grep -Fq 'foldGeminiIntoAntigravityProvider' packages/web/scripts/publish-usage.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: publishing never shrinks a published provider/day older than the last two days; older rows may only grow, so pruned or compressed local sessions cannot erase history
  command: bunx tsx --test --test-name-pattern 'recomputes only the last two days' packages/web/test/publish-usage.test.ts
  tags: [implemented]

## design
- label: the web report uses the reference fonts, a flat background, dark heatmap cells, obvious desaturated-to-saturated usage steps, and text-only view controls
  command: grep -Fq 'family=Karla' packages/web/app/globals.css && grep -Fq 'family=Space+Grotesk' packages/web/app/globals.css && grep -Fq -- '--font-sans: "helveticaNeue", "Helvetica Neue";' packages/web/app/globals.css && grep -Fq -- '--font-heading: "Space Grotesk";' packages/web/app/globals.css && grep -Fq -- '--font-control: "Karla";' packages/web/app/globals.css && grep -Fq -- '--font-mono: "Ioskeley Mono";' packages/web/app/globals.css && ! sed -n '/^:root {/,/^}/p' packages/web/app/globals.css | grep -Eq 'Arial|Inter|sans-serif|ui-monospace|SFMono|Menlo|Monaco|Consolas' && grep -Fq 'background: var(--color-bg);' packages/web/app/globals.css && grep -Fq 'colorMode: "dark"' packages/web/scripts/publish-usage.ts && grep -Fq '"#202822", // nearly gray low usage' packages/cli/src/graph.ts && ! grep -Fq '<rect x="-2" y="-2"' .slopmeter-data/published/heatmap-last-year.svg && grep -Fq 'fill="#262626"' .slopmeter-data/published/heatmap-last-year.svg && grep -Fq 'fill="#22c55e"' .slopmeter-data/published/heatmap-last-year.svg && ! grep -Fq 'fill="#ffffff"' .slopmeter-data/published/heatmap-last-year.svg && ! grep -Fq 'fill="#bbf7d0"' .slopmeter-data/published/heatmap-last-year.svg && grep -Fq 'font-family="helveticaNeue, Helvetica Neue"' .slopmeter-data/published/heatmap-last-year.svg && ! grep -Fq 'font-family="helveticaNeue, Helvetica Neue, sans-serif"' .slopmeter-data/published/heatmap-last-year.svg && grep -Fq '.view-toggle {' packages/web/app/globals.css && ! sed -n '/^\\.view-toggle {/,/^}/p' packages/web/app/globals.css | grep -Eq 'border:|border-radius:|background:' && grep -Fq '.burn-view {' packages/web/app/globals.css && ! sed -n '/^\\.burn-view {/,/^}/p' packages/web/app/globals.css | grep -Eq 'border:|border-radius:|background:'
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the deployed web app serves the reference font assets from the root public font URLs
  command: test -f public/assets/fonts/helvetica-neue/HelveticaNeue-Roman.otf && test -f public/assets/fonts/helvetica-neue/HelveticaNeue-Medium.otf && test -f public/assets/fonts/helvetica-neue/HelveticaNeueBold.ttf && test -f public/assets/fonts/helvetica-neue/HelveticaNeueItalic.ttf && test -f public/assets/fonts/ioskeley-mono/IoskeleyMono-Regular.woff2 && test -f public/assets/fonts/ioskeley-mono/IoskeleyMono-Bold.woff2 && grep -Fq 'url("/assets/fonts/helvetica-neue/HelveticaNeue-Roman.otf")' packages/web/app/globals.css && grep -Fq 'url("/assets/fonts/ioskeley-mono/IoskeleyMono-Regular.woff2")' packages/web/app/globals.css
  tags: [implemented]
- label: Droid CLI uses a red-orange accent closer to #d46922 than pure red
  command: grep -Fq 'accent: "#d46922"' packages/web/lib/analytics.ts && grep -Fq '"#d46922", // Droid red-orange high usage' packages/cli/src/graph.ts
  tags: [implemented]

## tabs
- label: each web report tab is its own statically prerendered URL (/ for Harnesses, /models, /cost, /details) switched by client-side links, titled per tab like "Cost · Daily Usage", with unknown slugs returning 404
  command: bun test packages/web/test/daily-burn.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'tab routes' && grep -Fq 'export const dynamicParams = false;' 'packages/web/app/[view]/page.tsx' && grep -Fq 'export const dynamicParams = false;' 'app/[view]/page.tsx' && grep -Fq 'useSelectedLayoutSegment()' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && grep -Fq '<Link' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && grep -Fq 'template: "%s · Daily Usage"' packages/web/app/layout.tsx && grep -Fq 'template: "%s · Daily Usage"' app/layout.tsx && grep -Fq '<UsageShell>' app/layout.tsx
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the Details tab shows a daily burn chart of smooth stacked token areas per harness in provider accent colors, with 7d/30d/90d/1y ranges, a PEAK readout for the visible range, per-day hover tooltips, and a per-harness range table instead of provider cards
  command: bun test packages/web/test/daily-burn.test.ts && grep -Fq '<DetailsView analytics={analytics} />' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && grep -Fq '{ label: "1y", days: 365 }' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && grep -Fq 'data-details-tooltip={day.tooltip}' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && ! grep -Fq 'LegacyProviderCards' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && ! grep -Fq 'provider-card' packages/web/app/globals.css
  tags: [implemented]

## cost
- label: the web report exposes a Cost tab with harness totals as the canonical top-line spend and provider/model costs as a partition drill-down subtotal
  command: grep -Fq 'Cost' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && grep -Fq 'harnessTotalCostUsd' packages/web/lib/analytics.ts && grep -Fq 'modelTotalCostUsd' packages/web/lib/analytics.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the published web data bundle includes a generated cost payload computed by the publish path from the merged daily usage and @pydantic/genai-prices price data
  command: grep -Fq 'publishedCostPayload' packages/web/lib/published-data.generated.ts && grep -Fq 'writePublishedCostArtifact' packages/web/scripts/publish-usage.ts && grep -Fq '@pydantic/genai-prices' packages/web/lib/model-prices.ts && grep -Fq 'loadLatestModelPrices' packages/web/scripts/publish-usage.ts && ! grep -Fq 'refresh-cost-data' package.json
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the Cost tab lets users switch between harness and provider/model grouping, rank by cost tokens or cost per million tokens, limit visible rows, manually hide rows, and optionally show zero-cost entries
  command: grep -Fq 'CostGroupMode' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && grep -Fq 'costRankModes' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && grep -Fq 'Show zero-cost' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && grep -Fq 'cost-visible-toggle' packages/web/app/globals.css
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the Cost tab explains costs as API-price equivalents rather than actual subscription-plan billing
  command: grep -Fq 'API-price equivalent' packages/web/scripts/lib/cost-analysis.ts && grep -Fq 'subscription plans' packages/web/lib/published-data.generated.ts
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the Cost tab visually separates filter groups for grouping ranking visibility and zero-cost controls
  command: grep -Fq 'cost-controls__group' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx && grep -Fq '.cost-controls__group + .cost-controls__group' packages/web/app/globals.css
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the Cost tab defaults to showing all visible cost rows instead of a top-N subset
  command: grep -Fq 'useState<CostVisibleLimit>("all")' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx
  tags: [implemented]
- label: published cost prices every provider/day/model breakdown row with cached input, cache writes, and unpriced models reported as missing-cost instead of guessed, with no ccusage dependency
  command: bun test packages/web/test/cost-analysis.test.ts && ! grep -rqi 'ccusage' packages/web/scripts packages/web/lib/types.ts package.json
  tags: [implemented]
- label: the Cost tab provider/model rows show exact per-model costs that sum to canonical harness spend
  command: bun test packages/web/test/usage.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'exact per-model costs'
  tags: [implemented]

- label: Details groups daily usage by harness, canonical model, or creator family; known aliases use provider colors and unknown models remain distinct with a neutral color
  command: bun test packages/web/test/daily-burn.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'model family grouping' && grep -Fq 'aria-label="Usage grouping"' packages/web/app/svg-usage.tsx
  tags: [implemented]
